From 68d317b789f4b5d31fcefef70550f1f80f77e0c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:41:28 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(sim): the app holders carry stock as CarriedStock,
 on either engine

camcraft-sim gains CarriedStock (Column(Body) | Field(FieldBody)): build,
carry, clip, simulate and one read-back onto the column body, so deviate,
display, volume and bounds stay the column carry's own code on both arms.
The app's holders - stock_sim_carry's Held and walk, rest/across's sweep,
rest's prior_state and PriorPlan - hold Stock / CarriedStock instead of
Dexel / Body. The column engine stays the default, call for call, so every
shipped verdict, golden and stamp is unchanged; the engine is a per-thread
choice (stock_sim::with_carry_engine, CAMCRAFT_CARRY_ENGINE=field).

The field arm is a closed solid over the stock grid's own lattice (a
verdict column is a field cell centre). Its clip is the column law as a
solid (minus the prism above the entered stock's top), not an
intersection that would delete what stands beside the new block. A
column cut through reads the stock's own extent, both ends finite, so the
verdict convicts it instead of reading air. A cylinder stock is refused
by name on the field arm (its mesh holds less than the round).

Pinned by sim carried_stock (6) and the heavy lane
carried_engine_agreement (release, --ignored): 14 documents of the
setup_carry, rest_across_setups and carried_verify fixtures read on both
engines, 0 findings.

Refs #637

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
